359 0 obj
<<
/Title (Thecase study demonstrated the major limitations that arise when low-code platforms are applied to complex)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 286 0 R
/Next 360 0 R
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Title (enterprise requirements: performance and scalability, complex business logic, system integration, extreme UX customisation, security and governance, AI / ML and advanced technology, vendor or platform dependency, and heavy data transformations. It also showed how a three-tier hybrid architecture of a low-code application, pro-code extensions and enterprise systems can address requirements beyond standard low-code capabilities.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 286 0 R
/Prev 359 0 R
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Title (Low-code platforms offer speed and simplicity for standard business applications, but their limitations become more significant as enterprise complexity increases. The trade-off is clear: low-code gives fast delivery, lower cost and wider participation in development, in exchange for ceilings in scale, logic, integration, customisation, governance and platform independence. For the Event Registration & Participant Management System, the standard functionality can be built quickly with low-code, while demanding requirements in logic, integration, security, scale and advanced technology need pro-code extensions connected to core enterprise systems.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 287 0 R
/Next 362 0 R
>>
endobj
362 0 obj
<<
/Title (A hybrid architecture keeps the speed of low-code for the standard layer and adds the flexibility of custom code where it is needed, which is why it is regarded as the practical standard for scalable enterprise platforms. It is therefore important to understand the limitations of a platform before selecting a development approach, so that the chosen approach matches the requirements of the enterprise application.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 287 0 R
/Prev 361 0 R
>>
endobj
